<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Showers seen over coastal Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Showers seen over coastal Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Tuesday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Bowathenna		0</p>
<p>    Canyon		   30.8</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    15.7</p>
<p>    Kotmale		  11.2</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 12.0</p>
<p>    Moussakele	     12.4</p>
<p>    Norton		    9.5</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     5.7</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	   15.0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   8.5</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
<p>The department forecast that thundershowers will be experienced along eastern coast on Wednesday morning. It said thundershowers will develop inland later in the day and spread to the west coast later.</p>
</text>
